{
  "dom_id": "step-q39773",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "If $‖3x‖=4$, find $‖\\frac{x}{5}‖.$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kx‖=|k|\\cdot ‖x‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3x‖ & =4 \\\\ |3|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =4 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $‖\\frac{x}{5}‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\frac{x}{5}‖ & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
